---
<div class="trickster-portraits">
  <figure><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-portrait.webp')} alt="Male Trickster portrait from Refuge" width="782" height="760" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Male Trickster</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-female-portrait.webp')} alt="Female Trickster portrait from Refuge" width="677" height="760" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Female Trickster</figcaption></figure>
</div>

<h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
<p>Trickster is a short-range, high-damage scythe job from Niflheim, combining quick attack rotations, critical hits, Fire skills, and life leech.</p>
<p>Refuge's class page notes that Hellraiser enables <strong>Finisher Ready</strong> without requiring level 10, and Sweeping Slash gains a third hit while that state is active.</p>

<h2 id="job-change">Job Change Quest</h2>
<Callout title="Requirement">
  <p><strong>Orphan Job Level 10</strong></p>
  <ol class="trickster-quest-steps">
    <li>
      <p>Speak with <strong>Lorelei Sorin</strong> in the Orphanage at <strong>va_orpha 376, 129</strong> and choose the cold-hearted answer.</p>
      <figure><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-job-change-lorelei.png')} alt="Lorelei Sorin in the Orphanage" width="140" height="150" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Lorelei Sorin</figcaption></figure>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Touch the <strong>Wisp</strong> at <strong>va_orpha 391, 133</strong> to enter the hidden chamber.</p>
      <figure><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-job-change-wisp.png')} alt="The Wisp in Lorelei's room" width="90" height="100" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Wisp</figcaption></figure>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Find <strong>Trickster Serin</strong> in the crypt at <strong>que_trck01 197, 198</strong> and win her number-guessing game.</p>
      <figure><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-job-change-serin.png')} alt="Trickster Serin in the crypt" width="160" height="230" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Trickster Serin</figcaption></figure>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="trickster-quest-reward">
    <p><strong>Reward:</strong> the Trickster job and a <strong>Black Scythe</strong>.</p>
    <picture><source media="(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)" srcset={withBase('images/classes/trickster-attacking-still.webp')} /><img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-attacking.webp')} alt="Trickster attacking" width="140" height="140" loading="lazy" /></picture>
  </div>
</Callout>

<h2 id="core-gameplay">Core Gameplay & Skills</h2>
<ul>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" /><strong>Scythe Reap:</strong> the opener for Trickster's main combo. It deals multiple hits and grants <strong>Combo Ready</strong>.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" /><strong>Sweeping Slash:</strong> cast it after Scythe Reap while <strong>Combo Ready</strong> is active. Without it, Sweeping Slash deals reduced damage.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="SN_SIGHT" /><strong>True Sight:</strong> grants +3 to all stats and +3 Hit and Critical per skill level. Keep it active to boost this STR/LUK build's damage and accuracy.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="RK_IGNITIONBREAK" /><strong>Hellraiser:</strong> a Fire attack around you with a long cooldown. It activates <strong>Finisher Ready</strong>.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="SA_FLAMELAUNCHER" /><strong>Burning Scythe:</strong> endows your weapon with Fire for its duration.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LK_PARRYING" /><strong>Shadow Parry:</strong> keep it active to block physical hits while using a scythe, with a brief pause after a successful block.</li>
</ul>
<p>This guide follows the STR/LUK damage build. Dark Message and Dark Messenger are INT-build skills and are not covered here.</p>
<h3>Early leveling (levels 1–100)</h3>
<p>Use this stat allocation example as a guide:</p>
<ol class="trickster-stat-order">
  <li>49 STR/LUK</li>
  <li>20 VIT/INT</li>
  <li>70 STR/LUK</li>
  <li>40 VIT/INT</li>
  <li>90 LUK</li>
</ol>
<p>Raise both STR and LUK to 49 before moving on to the later targets. Add VIT and INT as needed for survivability and SP while leveling.</p>
<p>It lists this skill order for Trickster:</p>
<ol class="trickster-skill-order">
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Unlock Scythe Reap and <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="PR_MACEMASTERY" />Max Scythe Mastery.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="MG_SRECOVERY" />Raise Increase SP Recovery to level 5.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Max Sweeping Slash.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="SN_SIGHT" />Max True Sight.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="MG_SRECOVERY" />Max Increase SP Recovery.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LK_PARRYING" />Max Shadow Parry.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Max Scythe Reap.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="SA_FLAMELAUNCHER" />Max Burning Scythe to endow your weapon with Fire; if you will not use it for that, spend those points leveling <SkillIcon icon="RK_IGNITIONBREAK" />Hellraiser instead.</li>
</ol>
<figure class="trickster-build-image">
  <img src={withBase('images/classes/trickster-skill-tree.png')} alt="Basic Trickster skill tree" width="562" height="403" loading="lazy" />
  <figcaption>Basic Trickster skill tree.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2 id="how-to-play">How to Play</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Keep <SkillIcon icon="SN_SIGHT" />True Sight active for its stat, Hit, and Critical bonuses.</li>
  <li>Keep <SkillIcon icon="LK_PARRYING" />Shadow Parry active to block physical hits while wielding a scythe.</li>
  <li>Use <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap to activate <strong>Combo Ready</strong>, then follow with <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash. Casting Sweeping Slash without <strong>Combo Ready</strong> reduces its damage.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="RK_IGNITIONBREAK" />Hellraiser has a long cooldown, but activates <strong>Finisher Ready</strong>, letting Sweeping Slash hit three times instead of two.</li>
  <li>Use <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap and <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash to deal damage; your scythe's leech restores HP as those skills hit. Watch SP and cooldowns during longer fights.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="leveling-spots">Leveling Spots</h2>
<p>See the <a href={withBase('guides/leveling-spots/')}>Leveling Spots</a> guide for monster ranges, routes, and location notes.</p>

